// The per-channel MMIO operation model (docs/wb_dma_operation_model.md §3).
//
// Every operation the processor initiates against ONE DMA channel lives here.
// The engine-global operations -- PAUSE, interrupt routing, descriptor memory
// -- live on wb_dma_ops_c, which owns an array of these.
//
// Why per-channel components rather than a `chan` parameter on every function:
//
//   The completion condition is a channel register, so an operation is a loop
//   over an indexed register access. Making the channel an instance rather than
//   an index keeps every access in the operation code index-free
//   (`regs.csr.read()`), which is both clearer and safer than indexing a
//   register array with a runtime value. It also matches the review decision
//   that operations are per-channel and a waking thread reads its own channel's
//   status register (§3.1.1).
//
//   The cost is that each channel binds its own top-level register group to its
//   own region -- see \init below.
//
// Every operation here is BLOCKING in the caller's view: it returns when the
// thing it names has completed. The wait points are not an implementation
// detail to be undone later; they are the specification of the driver state
// machine this model projects to (§2.3).

import addr_reg_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_regs_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_types_pkg::*;

component wb_dma_ch_ops_c {

    // Which channel this is, in dma_req_i/dma_ack_o and INT_SRC bit numbering.
    int                 chan;

    // Build-time capabilities. An absent capability makes the corresponding
    // control bit silently ignored by hardware, so operations consult this
    // rather than assuming everything is present.
    wb_dma_ch_caps_s    caps;

    // This channel's MMIO register bank. A top-level register group: it is
    // bound to its own non-allocatable region, not nested inside the device's
    // global group.
    wb_dma_ch_regs_c    regs;

    // Bind the bank. Called from wb_dma_ops_c's own init, which is called from
    // pss_top's exec init_down -- component attributes are only mutable during
    // initialization, and set_handle() is only legal from an init exec.
    // NOTE the space after `\init` -- an escaped identifier is terminated by
    // whitespace, so `\init(` would lex as a single token.
    solve function void \init (int id, addr_handle_t bank) {
        chan = id;
        regs.set_handle(bank);
    }
}
